m:1px solid black;" data-ref="095038ce-04ca-4475-b23a-4c853fd83847" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="d8ae032e-2d7e-4aa8-8711-e6f29b1cdbde"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="0406a9a7-8599-44ac-a803-0d0fdb1591ba"><p data-ref="ecfc11f4-b6de-4e4e-a6c6-eb9064e37b47" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">You are required to write a C program that computes the shortest paths from a source vertex to all other vertices in a weighted, directed graph. The program should utilize Dijkstra's algorithm to solve this problem.</p><p data-ref="bd140582-5529-44d0-ba6f-85845b1c5454" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="3cecfc8b-cdb1-4fca-b111-406c67d132b2"></p><p data-ref="b9bd3120-8271-4178-88b1-f9c14d2453e6" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="f2010904-d606-45cc-baa7-d5f4c478f061">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="93486e8e-08e9-43a7-bc35-e5b9874dd423" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="4e1a20d3-508b-4609-b411-e516d7507412">The first line contains two integers <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;" data-ref="41155ecd-b5ea-4bf8-8815-7f835c52cbc7" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="6aeb5d1f-a67a-4307-9354-394841dcca7d"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="a6a6265b-155a-4a63-85a1-4e1d0abdeec3"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D449 TEX-I" data-ref="fe608555-d951-42c6-9524-92b7ecf9ff95"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="a6f834eb-0ac6-491c-8e26-247f1edbbdb0"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="3296fa28-dacf-451c-98c2-4636a18333e2"><mi data-ref="3c78655f-3ed4-4706-aaa9-566970019ab8">V</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> and <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;" data-ref="bb6e514f-faa4-4399-a908-f6a16855a4c8" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="43d51959-b483-4111-a07d-c730414bd5a3"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="1b44db1e-0e2d-48a0-b586-f50f551e863d"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D438 TEX-I" data-ref="d5600213-7774-411e-8e3e-03d0e224863b"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="c9493cab-7e1e-453e-9717-294527966fe7"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="98a1f1de-4e4e-485a-ba5e-78887c9f34ec"><mi data-ref="57db828d-8cfe-49d0-9739-45eb5945e2a8">E</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, representing the number of vertices and the number of edges respectively.</li><li data-ref="d32d8b75-3273-4426-bd56-49690f8aa368">The next <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;" data-ref="8101fba5-768b-4e34-b7b4-d4e9478369bb" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="b9341c29-ce90-418c-bc3d-8e2021eafbcc"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="c532bc36-15e2-45ed-a6e9-38abc79b8c55"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D438 TEX-I" data-ref="7164f915-f7a0-45a5-97f3-589e5e88e31e"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="a914e972-be24-4911-8943-438bb3aa4078"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="59e0d8fa-5b2a-4614-aade-da3d8957b00d"><mi data-ref="70609fa1-eac0-47df-acb5-00f4367c97d4">E</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> lines each contain three integers <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;" data-ref="4ceca819-5c1c-43de-8390-6b3e2c694c39" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="2fefc98a-f1b9-4aa7-a654-1f006fd58bfc"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="6748d9aa-4540-4304-8284-8c4d1eb3c8de"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D462 TEX-I" data-ref="20577b55-3d86-4eac-9e66-0b6284f8deff"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="79d6d29c-97bc-4d40-b033-be68931e1647"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="0f634328-8a37-4be3-b12d-fcc9764f6205"><mi data-ref="a46d92fb-3763-4c8a-8d27-c5b9fa7b6756">u</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;" data-ref="ccea689e-005e-4e78-a32c-e4f4bfa6b3cb" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="bb0cfe46-5bcf-4ec7-8820-9ab31101ba60"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="a023f285-cf51-4f77-8102-4b6e5009e777"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D463 TEX-I" data-ref="b256058f-b815-40a3-a447-e778e980645d"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="6d18bb0b-1cb4-47ee-a8ec-6230e917e2e5"><ma