lid black;" data-ref="943930fa-921c-40d5-8cf6-b6a27a98f732" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="140129a2-94de-45ca-bf02-c7d62d308cdf"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="8954c595-8197-4fb7-992b-73f6f628eaa0"><p data-ref="948956ca-633a-4d23-a137-7df8fd7e6cf9" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a C program to solve the 0/1 Knapsack Problem using backtracking approach. The program aims to maximize the total value of items that can be included in a knapsack without exceeding its capacity</p><p data-ref="4a00765e-0b79-4415-aeba-caa0c7186a52" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="ff385d7a-63fc-4856-816a-1fe61e2d8914"></p><p data-ref="14d8f180-2e43-4285-9d34-08c3bdbb3d87" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="32f97b87-5c39-4328-8ea7-4323b074d0ea">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="f1c8f6bc-0df3-4613-994a-65643795a854" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="0325853b-5758-4668-9d36-48a6a4d352c2">The first line contains an integer <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;" data-ref="78e47245-d7e0-49d3-bca6-5803b1ca9ad4" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="a3d7d12f-55ef-46e2-8124-224bc7ea53c9"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="7aeae06d-1faa-4c0a-8b02-871f063b97d5"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="5237ad20-eb53-476f-8139-761f8fa9709e"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="6d0c5833-c379-4441-97ff-082169d332cd"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="b9135eb8-9529-41cf-a482-c754b48b437d"><mi data-ref="140592ab-e400-4918-8359-811db732f58e">n</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, representing the number of items.</li><li data-ref="27ed1520-f928-48b8-906e-a7dda6244ca3">The next <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;" data-ref="7fa164e0-b0b7-431d-81ad-1357cc440447" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="7f81c184-2970-442a-99a8-65993398c015"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="2bc59e09-dc94-4bd5-bc28-5eb875be1ef8"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="325912ff-3069-48ad-a663-014aed9b267a"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="12c42e31-7f0a-4542-bc7f-05db47a195a4"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="a7534a71-1c61-403f-923c-8acef3238779"><mi data-ref="9a564198-b303-4def-abd9-56e4c55fd590">n</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> lines each contain two space-separated integers: the value and weight of an item.</li><li data-ref="914fbc71-f135-40ec-85e4-05ceb04bc1b1">The last line contains an integer <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;" data-ref="39710f1e-acfb-4615-83e8-6ed0e6ebba58" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="ccd8eae9-fd29-432a-995d-52e6606de632"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="0c25194f-768e-4c18-b483-b4a019e835b8"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D44A TEX-I" data-ref="3b3285f6-77d1-4581-b08f-f0285ac6c8c1"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="aab12d7e-9513-4d67-8d05-7f45eea50c0b"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="d87ef941-0d82-4c6a-8a42-1679e064a40f"><mi data-ref="83245f22-8d52-4b56-9a1c-461f46e410c8">W</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, representing the capacity of the knapsack.</li></ul><p data-ref="bdef4fc6-0c70-4364-8ee1-964b5a860d51" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="8f00d1f9-dff8-4a73-a583-0d3581d882e3"></p><p data-ref="0459b6bb-1d47-445c-853e-76b81d62ec5e" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="344e308a-3845-4343-a4ba-66be266d6f80">Output Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="3a64cc23-71c2-4d76-8ff8-57ec9198aa9d" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="a89e8f9a-a4fc-4229-8d27-97705599b195">Print the maximum profit (total value) that can be obtained by selecting items, considering the knapsack's capacity constraint.</li></ul><p data-ref="9de3806b-a8cb-4417-b816-8defdda052ec" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="d3f11a7a-48bd-403d-a978-37e27f85bbb4"></p><p data-ref="1f1cffdc-4d55-4ec6-827e-33dfe24b7403" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="8a284fd6-b4cf-4a6c-b6c9-2f3593b86f9e">Note:</strong> Refer to the test cases for better understanding.</p></span></div><div class="mb-3" data-ref="a845f68e-5b9c-4b73-8a73-71c2071b0372" data-split-to="a845f68e-5b9c-4b73-8a73-71c2071b0372" data-split-original="true" data-last-split-element="true" data-align-last-split-element="auto"><div class="ml-1 mb-3" data-ref="d5a46e56-b43f-4882-9ead-1c2050ff318d"><b style="border-bottom:1px solid black;" data-ref="53ce19a0-f29c-43cc-bfcd-dc71591a0802" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Source Code: </b></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
